g good morning this is another  example of where investigators just  jumped too fast on the first suspect and  I see that over and over again in this  well one thing I'm wondering from your  report if Michael was released from  parole why are his attorneys now  fighting to get him another hearing form  get him back in court well because he  was released on Pro but that means he's  a convicted felon a convicted killer  um he wants to clear his name and he  says he wants to get Justice for his  mother because I mean a lot of people  wonder did he do it or did he not even  though he's out why did police zero in  on him so quickly well I mean they  should have at least looked at him I  mean he was in the house when his mom  died and they thought he acted a little  inappropriately when they were taken him  to the Sheriff's Office he asked who's  going to get my mother's truck but his  sister said that's all his mother had so  it was a normal thing and they ignored  the fact or didn't take seriously enough  the fact that there wasn't real physical  evidence I mentioned no weapon there was  no time to get rid of a weapon she  fought her attacker he had no injuries  no blood on him but he he also was a  troubled child so they focused on him  and it was kind of over after that well  real treat to get to see you two days in  a row but a very interesting case uh  folks can see the case against Michael  polite on 48 hours tomorrow night at 10  Central oh sorry 10 9 Central right here  on CBS and Paramount Plus
 

